    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2026.106302",
      "sequence": 8,
      "source_sequence": 8,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Identification-robust inference for the LATE with high-dimensional covariates",
      "title_cn": "具有高维协变量的 LATE 的识别鲁棒推理",
      "authors": [
        "Yukun Ma"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "This paper investigates the local average treatment effect (LATE) with high-dimensional covariates, irrespective of the strength of identification. We propose a novel test statistic for the high-dimensional LATE and demonstrate that our test has uniformly correct asymptotic size. By employing the double/debiased machine learning method for nuisance parameter estimation, we develop easy-to-implement algorithms for inference and confidence interval calculation of the high-dimensional LATE. Simulations indicate that our test is robust against both weak identification and high dimensionality concerning size control and power performance, outperforming other conventional tests. Applying the proposed method to railroad and population data to study the effect of railroad access on urban population growth, we observe that our methodology yields point estimates for the railroad access coefficients that are smaller in magnitude and confidence intervals that are by 49% to 92% shorter depending on specifications, when compared to the conventional results.",
      "abstract_cn": "本文研究了高维协变量的局部平均治疗效果（LATE），无论识别的强度如何。我们提出了一种新的高维 LATE 检验统计量，并证明我们的检验具有一致正确的渐近大小。通过采用双/去偏机器学习方法进行干扰参数估计，我们开发了易于实现的算法，用于高维 LATE 的推理和置信区间计算。模拟表明，我们的测试在尺寸控制和功率性能方面对于弱识别和高维都具有鲁棒性，优于其他传统测试。将所提出的方法应用于铁路和人口数据，以研究铁路通达对城市人口增长的影响，我们观察到，与传统结果相比，我们的方法产生的铁路通达系数的点估计值较小，并且根据规格的置信区间较短 49% 至 92%。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jeconom.2026.106302",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304407626001235?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
      "publication_date": "September 2026",
      "sources": {
        "issue": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-econometrics/vol/257/suppl/C",
        "roster": "https://rss.sciencedirect.com/publication/science/03044076",
        "metadata": "crossref",
        "abstract_en": "semantic-scholar",
        "abstract_lookup": {
          "status": "insufficient_entitlement",
