    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2026.106298",
      "sequence": 9,
      "source_sequence": 9,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Flexible covariate adjustments in regression discontinuity designs",
      "title_cn": "断点回归设计中灵活的协变量调整",
      "authors": [
        "Claudia Noack",
        "Tomasz Olma",
        "Christoph Rothe"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Empirical regression discontinuity (RD) studies often include covariates in their specifications to increase the precision of their estimates. In this paper, we propose a novel class of estimators that use such covariate information more efficiently than existing methods and can accommodate many covariates. Our estimators are simple to implement and involve running a standard RD analysis after subtracting a function of the covariates from the original outcome variable. We characterize the function of the covariates that minimizes the asymptotic variance of these estimators. We also show that the conventional RD framework gives rise to a special robustness property which implies that the optimal adjustment function can be estimated flexibly via modern machine learning techniques without affecting the first-order properties of the final RD estimator. We demonstrate our methods' scope for efficiency improvements by reanalyzing data from a large number of recently published empirical studies.",
      "abstract_cn": "经验回归不连续性 (RD) 研究通常在其规范中包含协变量，以提高估计的精度。在本文中，我们提出了一类新颖的估计器，它比现有方法更有效地使用此类协变量信息，并且可以容纳许多协变量。我们的估计器很容易实现，并且需要在从原始结果变量中减去协变量函数后运行标准 RD 分析。我们描述了最小化这些估计量的渐近方差的协变量函数。我们还表明，传统的 RD 框架产生了一种特殊的鲁棒性属性，这意味着可以通过现代机器学习技术灵活地估计最优调整函数，而不影响最终 RD 估计器的 第一 阶属性。我们通过重新分析大量最近发表的实证研究的数据来证明我们的方法提高效率的范围。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jeconom.2026.106298",
