    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2026.106307",
      "sequence": 13,
      "source_sequence": 13,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Regression adjustment in completely randomized experiments with many covariates",
      "title_cn": "具有许多协变量的完全随机实验的回归调整",
      "authors": [
        "Harold D. Chiang",
        "Yukitoshi Matsushita",
        "Taisuke Otsu"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "This paper investigates estimation and inference for average treatment effects in completely randomized experiments when researchers observe potentially many covariates. Within Neyman's (1923) design-based framework, allowing the number of covariates to grow more slowly than the sample size, we demonstrate that a cross-fitted regression adjustment estimator--adapted from Aronow and Middleton (2013)--exhibits more favorable asymptotic properties than existing alternatives, such as Lin's (2013) regression adjustment estimator and the bias-corrected estimator of Lei and Ding (2021). For inference, we derive the first- and second-order terms in the stochastic expansions of regression-adjusted estimators, analyze the higher-order behavior of existing inference procedures, and introduce a modified version of the HC3 standard error. The proposed methods extend naturally to stratified experiments with large strata. Simulation studies show that the cross-fitted estimator, in combination with the modified HC3, provides accurate point estimates and reliable size control across a wide range of data-generating processes.",
      "abstract_cn": "本文研究了当研究人员观察到潜在的许多协变量时，在完全随机的实验中对平均治疗效果的估计和推断。在 Neyman（1923）基于设计的框架内，允许协变量数量的增长速度比样本大小更慢，我们证明了交叉拟合回归调整估计量（改编自 Aronow 和 Middleton（2013））比现有替代方案（例如 Lin（2013）回归调整估计量和偏差校正）表现出更有利的渐近特性。 Lei 和 Ding 的估计量（2021）。为了进行推理，我们推导了回归调整估计量的随机展开式中的 第一 和 第二 阶项，分析了现有推理过程的高阶行为，并引入了 HC3 标准误差的修改版本。所提出的方法自然地扩展到大地层的分层实验。仿真研究表明，交叉拟合估计器与修改后的 HC3 相结合，可以在各种数据生成过程中提供准确的点估计和可靠的大小控制。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
